WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:10.830
ANC Studio’s Proposal workspace turns project requirements into an estimate package. Start with your source documents, then review the price and prepare the client delivery.

2
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:19.998
Drop in an RFP or a pricing workbook. Add the client, project, and any instructions, then select Build proposal package.

3
00:00:20.598 --> 00:00:29.636
Review Scope and pricing. Check each display’s width, height, pixel pitch, quantity, and installation. Missing details stay highlighted until you complete them.

4
00:00:30.236 --> 00:00:38.543
The finished estimate uses ANC branding and shows the project total. Read the PDF in the workspace, or download it for review.

5
00:00:39.143 --> 00:00:50.480
RFPs and briefs use ANC estimating rates. A supplied pricing workbook keeps its selling prices. Budget estimates still need scope and supplier pricing review.

6
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:58.839
Use the page arrows to check the technical specifications. Keep the source documents with the proposal so you can trace the requirements.

7
00:00:59.439 --> 00:01:08.163
Download the internal cost workbook for your team. Create a client link for the completed PDF version you want to share. You can revoke that link.

8
00:01:08.763 --> 00:01:17.932
The client sees an ANC estimate. Internal workbooks stay private. Later revisions create new versions without changing a PDF you already shared.

